BUG REPORT: `Context#Scheme()` (in /echo/context.go) returns whatever string is in the `X-Forwarded-Proto` / `X-Forwarded-Protocol` / `X-Url-Scheme` request headers, even when the value is not a real HTTP scheme. Example:

```go
c.Request().Header.Set("X-Forwarded-Proto", "ftp")
c.Request().Header.Set("X-Url-Scheme", "https")
c.Scheme() // returns "ftp", expected "https"
```

Expected behavior: ignore a header value that is not a valid HTTP scheme and continue with the next header check; if no valid scheme is present, return "http". The Context interface documents Scheme as: "Scheme returns the HTTP protocol scheme, `http` or `https`." (see /echo/context.go).

CURRENT CODE (in /echo/context.go, around line 252):

```go
func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}
```

REQUIRED EDIT: keep the exact same precedence order and the same TLS / X-Forwarded-Ssl handling, but only accept a header value that is a valid HTTP scheme, i.e. "http" or "https" compared case-insensitively (use `strings.EqualFold`; `strings` is already imported in context.go). Return the header value unchanged when it is valid. Add a small unexported helper next to Scheme, e.g.:

```go
// isHTTPScheme reports whether the given value is a valid HTTP scheme, i.e. `http` or `https`.
func isHTTPScheme(scheme string) bool {
	return strings.EqualFold(scheme, "http") || strings.EqualFold(scheme, "https")
}
```

and use `if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); isHTTPScheme(scheme) { return scheme }` etc. for HeaderXForwardedProto, HeaderXForwardedProtocol and HeaderXUrlScheme. Do not change any other function. Keep the file gofmt-clean.

