Go repo at /echo (module github.com/labstack/echo/v4, middleware package). Fix a reported bug in /echo/middleware/compress.go (the Gzip middleware). Do NOT modify any existing *_test.go file. You may create a temp test file but must delete it afterwards. Other agents are concurrently editing /echo/context.go, /echo/bind.go, /echo/router.go, /echo/echo.go, /echo/group.go — do not touch those.

BUG: with `e.Use(Gzip())` and a handler that returns an empty body with 200, e.g. `e.GET("/empty", func(c echo.Context) error { return c.String(http.StatusOK, "") })` and a client sending `Accept-Encoding: gzip`, the response has NO `Content-Encoding: gzip` header but the body IS binary gzip data (gzip magic bytes), so clients show garbage. Expected: either a valid gzip stream WITH `Content-Encoding: gzip` (and `Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8`), or no gzip body at all.

ROOT CAUSE: in `GzipWithConfig` the deferred func runs `w.Reset(ioutil.Discard)` when `res.Size == 0` (so the gzip trailer is discarded) but then ALWAYS calls `w.Close()`. When the handler wrote an empty string, `res.Size` is 0 even though the response was committed and the gzip header (written by the first `Write`) already went to the real writer, while `Content-Encoding` was deleted because Size == 0. Result: gzip bytes with no Content-Encoding header.

REQUIRED EDIT: in the deferred func, close the gzip writer into the discarded writer when nothing was written, and otherwise close it so the gzip stream is properly finished on the real response writer. Replace:

```go
				defer func() {
					if res.Size == 0 {
						if res.Header().Get(echo.HeaderContentEncoding) == gzipScheme {
							res.Header().Del(echo.HeaderContentEncoding)
						}
						// We have to reset response to it's pristine state when
						// nothing is written to body or error is returned.
						// See issue #424, #407.
						res.Writer = rw
						w.Reset(ioutil.Discard)
					}
					w.Close()
					pool.Put(w)
				}()
```

with:

```go
				defer func() {
					if res.Size == 0 {
						if res.Header().Get(echo.HeaderContentEncoding) == gzipScheme {
							res.Header().Del(echo.HeaderContentEncoding)
						}
						// We have to reset response to it's pristine state when
						// nothing is written to body or error is returned.
						// See issue #424, #407.
						res.Writer = rw
						w.Reset(ioutil.Discard)
						// Nothing was written to the response body, so the gzip stream must not be
						// written to the client (it would be unreadable binary data without a
						// `Content-Encoding` header). Finish the stream into the discarded writer.
						w.Close()
					} else {
						// Response body was written, so finish the gzip stream on the real writer.
						w.Close()
					}
					pool.Put(w)
				}()
```

(You may simplify to a single `w.Close()` after the if/else as long as the `w.Reset(ioutil.Discard)` still happens before the close in the Size == 0 branch. Keep gofmt clean.)

